# Postman JSON Collection Generation Rules

## File Structure

Each module in the API should have its own JSON file in `http/` folder (e.g., `authentication.json`, `class-registration.json`, `task.json`, `email.json`, `inquiry.json`).

## Collection Format

```json
{
  "info": {
    "name": "<Module Name>",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    // Group endpoints by resource
  ]
}
```

## Endpoint Request Format

### GET Request (with query params)

```json
{
  "name": "<endpointName>",
  "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "url": {
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["module", "resources", ":id"],
      "query": [
        { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
        { "key": "limit", "value": "10" },
        { "key": "keyword", "value": "", "disabled": true },
        { "key": "orderCol", "value": "id", "description": "id | field1 | field2 | createdAt | updatedAt" },
        { "key": "orderDir", "value": "DESC", "description": "ASC | DESC" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### GET Request (with path variable)

```json
{
  "name": "findOne",
  "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "url": {
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["module", "resources", ":id"],
      "variable": [
        { "key": "id", "value": "1" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### POST Request

```json
{
  "name": "create",
  "request": {
    "method": "POST",
    "body": {
      "mode": "raw",
      "options": {
        "raw": {
          "language": "json"
        }
      },
      "raw": "{\n    \"field\": \"value\"\n}"
    },
    "url": {
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["module", "resources"]
    }
  }
}
```

### PUT Request

```json
{
  "name": "update",
  "request": {
    "method": "PUT",
    "body": {
      "mode": "raw",
      "options": {
        "raw": {
          "language": "json"
        }
      },
      "raw": "{\n    \"field\": \"newValue\"\n}"
    },
    "url": {
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["module", "resources", ":id"],
      "variable": [
        { "key": "id", "value": "1" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### DELETE Request

```json
{
  "name": "remove",
  "request": {
    "method": "DELETE",
    "url": {
      "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
      "path": ["module", "resources", ":id"],
      "variable": [
        { "key": "id", "value": "1" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Conventions

### 1. URL Format
- **DO NOT** use `raw` property in URL
- Use `host`, `path`, `query`, `variable` separately
- Path parameters use `:paramName` format

### 2. Headers
- **DO NOT** include empty `"header": []`
- Default headers are not needed

### 3. Body (JSON)
- When using `mode: "raw"` with JSON data, **MUST** add `"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }`
- Example:
  ```json
  "body": {
    "mode": "raw",
    "options": {
      "raw": {
        "language": "json"
      }
    },
    "raw": "{\n    \"field\": \"value\"\n}"
  }
  ```

### 4. Query Parameters
- Standard pagination: `page`, `limit`
- Search: `keyword` (disabled by default)
- Sorting: `orderCol`, `orderDir`
- Filter fields: add as needed with `disabled: true`

### 5. Descriptions
- **ONLY** use descriptions for enum values
- Format: `value1 | value2 | value3`
- Examples:
  - `orderCol`: `id | field1 | field2 | createdAt | updatedAt`
  - `orderDir`: `ASC | DESC`
  - `status`: `pending | approved | rejected`
  - `role`: `student | lecture | admin`

- **DO NOT** add descriptions for:
  - Date formats (e.g., "YYYY-MM-DD")
  - Data formats (e.g., "ISO date", "comma-separated IDs")
  - Generic field descriptions

### 6. Nested Resources
For nested endpoints (e.g., ClassRegistrationItems within ClassRegistrations):

```json
{
  "name": "ClassRegistrationItems",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "findAll",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": {
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["classRegistration", "classRegistrations", ":parentId", "items"],
          "variable": [
            { "key": "parentId", "value": "1" }
          ],
          "query": [
            { "key": "page", "value": "1" },
            { "key": "limit", "value": "10" }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

### 7. Grouping
- Group related endpoints under a parent `item`
- Use singular names for endpoint groups (e.g., `Users`, `ClassRegistrations`, not `User`, `ClassRegistration`)

